  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CICIG 2017-2020 International Commission Against Impunity in Guatemala - The International Commission Against Impunity in</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CICIG 2017-2020 Internationella Kommissionen mot Straffrihet i Guatemala</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den Internationella Kommissionen mot Straffrihet i Guatemala, CICIG, etablerades efter en v&#xe4;djan fr&#xe5;n Guatemala till FN om st&#xf6;d i kampen mot straffrihet.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Commission against Impunity in Guatemala (CICIG), was established upon request by Guatemala to the UN for support in the fight against impunity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Commission against Impunity in Guatemala (CICIG) was established in 2007 as an independent, international body designed to support the Attorney General&apos;s Office (MP), the National Civil Police (PNC) and other state institutions in the investigation and prosecution of illicit security forces and clandestine security organizations&#xa0; (CIACS).&#xa0;The mandate was was extended every two years, until the decision in 2019 by the Guatemalan government not to extend it, and the CICIG had to close in September 2019. &#xa0;
The mandate was comprised of three main objectives:  - to investigate the existence of CIACS that commit crimes that affect the fundamental human rights of the citizens of Guatemala, and identify the structures of these illegal groups (including the links between such groups and state officials) as well as their activities, operating modalities and sources of financin.  - to assist the state to disband CIACS, and promote the investigation, criminal prosecution and punishment of the crimes committed by the members of such groups.  - to make recommendations to the State of Guatemala regarding public policies to be adopted&#x2014;including the necessary judicial and institutional reforms&#x2014;to eradicate and prevent the re-emergence of CIACS.</narrative>
  </description>
